# Documentation Rules

This project follows a strict documentation structure to ensure clarity and maintainability.

## Directory Structure
All documentation must be located in the `doc/` directory at the project root.
The `doc/` directory must contain the following subdirectories:
- `api/`: For API specifications and endpoint definitions.
- `design/`: For UI/UX designs and design system guidelines.
- `requirements/`: For product requirements and user stories.
- `technical/`: For technical guides and setup instructions.

## Index File
- A `doc/index.md` file must exist and serve as the entry point for all documentation.
- When adding new documentation files, you MUST update `doc/index.md` to include a link and a brief description of the new file.

## Format
- All documentation must be written in Markdown (`.md`).

## Implementation Consistency
- When implementing code, ALWAYS refer back to the documentation in `doc/` to ensure consistency and maintainability.
- If the implementation deviates from the documentation, update the documentation to reflect the changes.

